# Analytics ids for LOCAL DEVELOPMENT — deliberately FAKE.
#
# Why this file exists: the consent drawer (§20.1) only appears in a build that
# actually carries analytics ids, because asking permission to collect nothing is
# noise, not diligence. The real ids live in `.env.production`, which `npm run
# dev` does not load — so without these placeholders the drawer is invisible on
# the dev server, which reads as the feature being broken rather than as it doing
# exactly what it was told.
#
# These ids belong to NO property: `G-DEV0000000` is not a Google Analytics
# measurement id that exists and `devlocal` is not a Clarity project. Nothing is
# loaded at all until Accept is pressed in the drawer, and what is sent after that
# is dropped by the vendors as unknown-id traffic. So the dev/prod gate still
# holds: development traffic cannot reach the real dashboards. NEVER put the real
# ids here — that is what `.env.production` is for, and the reasons are in it.
#
# `vitest` is unaffected: it runs in mode `test` and loads `.env.test*`, not this.
# Its analytics tests stub the env explicitly anyway.
VITE_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=G-DEV0000000
VITE_CLARITY_PROJECT_ID=devlocal
